{"name":"Dark Charcoal","hex":"#333232","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"charcoal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["impure carbon obtained by destructive distillation of wood or other organic matter, that is, heating it in the absence of oxygen.","A stick of black carbon material used for drawing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark gray colour.","Made of charcoal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charcoal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charcoal","blocks":[{"text":"Charcoal is a lightweight black residue made of carbon that is produced by strongly heating wood in minimal oxygen to remove all water and volatile constituents. In the traditional version of this pyrolysis process, called charcoal burning, often by forming a charcoal kiln, the heat is supplied by burning part of the starting material itself, with a limited supply of oxygen. The material can also be heated in a closed retort. Modern charcoal briquettes used for outdoor cooking may contain many other additives, e.g. coal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charcoal_8.jpg/330px-Charcoal_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charcoal"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"},{"title":"Shades of gray","blocks":[{"text":"Vari